# Tech Stack for Hetri PAW Market Platform

This document outlines the technologies and components used to build the Hetri PAW market platform, a Next.js application with PostgreSQL database, Electron desktop wrapper, real-time messaging, video streaming, and comprehensive facility management capabilities.

---

## 1. Core Application Platform

### Framework & Runtime

* **Next.js 14+** with App Router
  * React 18+ with TypeScript for type safety
  * File-based routing with `src/app/` directory structure
  * API routes for backend services (`/api/*`)
  * Static export capability for deployment flexibility

* **Node.js Environment**
  * Version 18+ for development and production
  * Package management via npm with lockfile consistency
  * Support for server-side PostgreSQL operations

### Frontend Architecture

* **React 18+** with modern hooks and concurrent features
  * Functional components with TypeScript interfaces
  * Custom hooks for business logic encapsulation (`useAuth`, `useDataPolling`)
  * Context providers for global state management

* **TypeScript** for complete type safety
  * Strict mode configuration
  * Interface definitions for all data structures
  * Generic types for reusable components and services

### Desktop Application

* **Electron 28+** for cross-platform desktop deployment
  * Main process with window management (`electron-main.js`)
  * Preload script for secure IPC communication
  * Auto-updater integration with GitHub releases
  * Window state management and system tray support

---

## 2. Database & Backend Architecture

### Primary Database

* **PostgreSQL 13+** (Complete replacement of localStorage/Firebase dual approach)
  * Connection pooling with `pg` driver
  * UUID-based primary keys with `uuid-ossp` extension
  * JSONB support for complex data structures
  * Advanced indexing and performance optimization
  * Full ACID compliance for booking validation

### Database Features

* **Enhanced Schema Design**
  * 15+ interconnected tables with foreign key constraints
  * Exclusion constraints to prevent double-booking
  * Comprehensive user roles (customer, admin, staff)
  * Detailed facility management with GPS coordinates
  * Camera tracking with viewer limits (1-3 concurrent)
  * TreatTap session management with time slots

* **Authentication & Security**
  * JWT-based authentication with HTTP-only cookies
  * BCrypt password hashing
  * Session management with expiration cleanup
  * Role-based access control (RBAC)
  * Invite code system for facility onboarding

### Backend Services

* **RESTful API Layer** (Next.js API Routes)
  * `/api/database/init` - Database initialization and schema
  * `/api/auth/*` - Authentication endpoints (login, register, logout)
  * `/api/paw-parents` - Customer management
  * `/api/paw-associates` - Staff management with online status
  * `/api/pets` - Pet profile management
  * `/api/facilities` - Facility management with services
  * `/api/analytics` - Real-time dashboard metrics
  * `/api/streaming` - Video streaming management
  * `/api/bookings/validate` - Booking validation service

---

## 3. Real-Time Communication & Streaming

### MQTT Messaging

* **MQTT 5.3+** for real-time TreatTap communication
  * Sub-100ms latency for treat requests
  * Facility-specific topic namespacing
  * Quality of Service (QoS) levels for reliability
  * Automatic reconnection with exponential backoff
  * Device status monitoring and heartbeat system

### Video Streaming Architecture

* **MJPEG Camera Integration**
  * IP camera support with configurable ports
  * HLS (HTTP Live Streaming) distribution
  * CloudFront CDN integration for global delivery
  * Concurrent viewer limits (1-3 per stream)
  * Stream analytics and usage tracking

* **Streaming Service Features**
  * Real-time viewer count management
  * Stream session logging and analytics
  * Camera heartbeat monitoring
  * Automatic offline detection
  * Quality adaptation (480p, 720p, auto)

### Caching & Performance

* **Redis 4.6+** for caching and session management
  * High-performance data caching
  * Session state persistence
  * Real-time data synchronization
  * Pub/Sub messaging support

